  <body
    class="spell-doc-page"
    data-set="spell"
    data-topic="app"
    data-short="app"
    data-n="6"
    data-icon="window maximize"
    data-accent="blue"
    data-status="draft"
  >
    <spell-site-header root="../../.."></spell-site-header>
    <div class="spell-doc">
      <main class="spell-doc-main">
        <!--
          TOPIC PAGE:  made by `yarn goals new`;  rules in `goals/AGENTS.md`.
          - Structured parts (items, status, history, updated) go through `yarn goals ...`;  hand-edit prose only.
          - Section ids are fixed:  other topics link to them.
        -->
        <ui-breadcrumb class="spell-crumbs" size="small" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <ui-breadcrumb-section href="../../index.html" target="_self">Goals</ui-breadcrumb-section>
          <ui-breadcrumb-section href="../index.html" target="_self">spell</ui-breadcrumb-section>
          <ui-breadcrumb-section active>6 · app</ui-breadcrumb-section>
        </ui-breadcrumb>
        <header class="goals-hero">
          <span class="goals-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true"><ui-icon name="window maximize"></ui-icon></span>
          <p class="goals-eyebrow"><span class="goals-num">6</span> Topic · app</p>
          <h1>The spell app</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            The editor where people write and run spells, and, soon, build them by dragging things around.
          </p>
          <ui-list class="spell-meta">
            <ui-item icon="flag"
              >Status: <ui-label class="goals-status" size="mini" color="grey">draft</ui-label> · first pass, not yet
              talked through</ui-item
            >
            <ui-item icon="calendar">Updated: <time class="goals-updated">2026-10-01</time></ui-item>
            <ui-item icon="robot">Notes for agents: <a href="app.md" target="src-goals-app-app-md">app.md</a></ui-item>
          </ui-list>
        </header>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="summary"><ui-icon name="eye"></ui-icon> 1. Summary</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Today:</strong> a web app (React, Monaco) that compiles as you type and runs the program beside
              your code, with the same language features as VS Code.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Strong core:</strong> the compiler runs in the browser; the server only reads and writes files.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Not yet for people:</strong> projects live inside the source tree, there's no file list, Help and
              About are stubs, and parser debug panes take half the screen.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Next:</strong> a friendlier shell, a "my projects" folder, then drag-and-drop editing.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="today"><ui-icon name="calendar"></ui-icon> 2. Today</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Where:</strong>
              <a href="../../../packages/app/" target="src-packages-app"><code>packages/app</code></a
              >: routes <code>/</code> (projects), <code>/edit/...</code>, <code>/run/...</code>; the editor page is
              <a
                href="../../../packages/app/src/pages/SpellEditor.tsx"
                target="src-packages-app-src-pages-spelleditor-tsx"
                ><code>packages/app/src/pages/SpellEditor.tsx</code></a
              >.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Editor page:</strong> Monaco and a console on the left; the running app, an AST viewer and a match
              viewer on the right; files from a dropdown. Compiles two seconds after you stop typing.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Serving:</strong> a vite dev server (:3000) plus an express file API (:3001);
              <code>yarn start</code> in
              <a href="../../../packages/app/" target="src-packages-app"><code>packages/app</code></a
              >.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Stubs:</strong> log in, publish, docs, about, help and project settings only log a TODO (<a
                href="../../../packages/app/src/editor.ts"
                target="src-packages-app-src-editor-ts"
                ><code>packages/app/src/editor.ts</code></a
              >).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>UI stack:</strong> React 18 and semantic-ui-react; a move to Solid and @spell-app/ui is planned
              but paused.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Explorers:</strong> the Type and Thing explorers exist, but only in
              <code>&lt;spell-app&gt;</code>'s debug pane and the VS Code runner.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Server safety:</strong> fine on localhost, not beyond it (<a
                href="../../../agents/SUSPECTED-BUGS.md"
                target="src-suspected-bugs-md"
                ><code>agents/SUSPECTED-BUGS.md</code></a
              >: no file locking, stack traces sent to the browser).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="goals"><ui-icon name="bullseye"></ui-icon> 3. Goals</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <section class="s3">
            <ui-sticky class="spell-h3"
              ><h3 id="now"><ui-icon name="seedling"></ui-icon> Now → December 2026</h3></ui-sticky
            >
            <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="goal" data-horizon="now">
              <li data-status="open" id="g1">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g1">G1</a>
                <span class="plan-title">A shell for people, not parser developers</span>
                <span class="goals-note">debug panes behind a switch; a file list; clear Run and Edit</span>
              </li>
              <li data-status="open" id="g2">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g2">G2</a> <span class="plan-title">My projects</span>
                <span class="goals-note">projects in your own folder; new, duplicate an example, rename, delete</span
                ><ui-accordion class="spell-aside" styled
                  ><ui-title>details</ui-title
                  ><ui-content
                    ><p>
                      Today
                      <a
                        href="../../../packages/spell/src/node/environment.ts"
                        target="src-packages-spell-src-node-environment-ts"
                        ><code>environment.ts</code></a
                      >
                      points at
                      <a href="../../../packages/spell/projects/" target="src-packages-spell-projects"
                        ><code>packages/spell/projects</code></a
                      >, and examples are edited in place.
                    </p>
                  </ui-content></ui-accordion
                >
              </li>
              <li data-status="open" id="g3">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g3">G3</a> <span class="plan-title">Guides inside the app</span>
                <span class="goals-note">the <code>@system:guides</code> root is configured but empty; see docs</span>
              </li>
              <li data-status="open" id="g4">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g4">G4</a> <span class="plan-title">Runs without a dev server</span>
                <span class="goals-note"
                  >a static build plus a storage adapter: the base for native and web-components</span
                >
              </li>
            </ol>
          </section>
          <section class="s3">
            <ui-sticky class="spell-h3"
              ><h3 id="next"><ui-icon name="tree"></ui-icon> 2027</h3></ui-sticky
            >
            <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="goal" data-horizon="next">
              <li data-status="open" id="g5">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g5">G5</a> <span class="plan-title">Drag-and-drop editing</span>
                <span class="goals-note">place <code>ui-*</code> components, set their properties, attach scripts</span
                ><ui-accordion class="spell-aside" styled
                  ><ui-title>details</ui-title
                  ><ui-content
                    ><p>
                      HyperCard's authoring level. @spell-app/ui's vocabulary files already describe every attribute and
                      value, which is most of a properties panel.
                    </p>
                  </ui-content></ui-accordion
                >
              </li>
              <li data-status="open" id="g6">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g6">G6</a> <span class="plan-title">Browse, author and script modes</span>
                <span class="goals-note">HyperCard's levels, as modes</span>
              </li>
              <li data-status="open" id="g7">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g7">G7</a> <span class="plan-title">Undo you can trust</span>
                <span class="goals-note">named snapshots and branches</span
                ><ui-accordion class="spell-aside" styled
                  ><ui-title>details</ui-title
                  ><ui-content
                    ><p>
                      From <code>_thoughts/editor needs to.md</code>: "Make it super super easy to name, branch and
                      restore state."
                    </p>
                  </ui-content></ui-accordion
                >
              </li>
            </ol>
          </section>
          <section class="s3">
            <ui-sticky class="spell-h3"
              ><h3 id="someday"><ui-icon name="mountain sun"></ui-icon> Someday</h3></ui-sticky
            >
            <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="goal" data-horizon="someday">
              <li data-status="open" id="g8">
                <a class="plan-id" href="#g8">G8</a> <span class="plan-title">The editor is a spell</span>
                <span class="goals-note">people can change the editor itself</span>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </section>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="ideas"><ui-icon name="lightbulb"></ui-icon> 4. Ideas</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="idea">
            <li data-status="open" id="i1">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#i1">I1</a> <span class="plan-title">Cmd-click to see the script</span>
              <span class="goals-note">anything on screen opens its spell</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="i2">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#i2">I2</a> <span class="plan-title">Every phrase shows what it does</span>
              <span class="goals-note"
                >type a line, see its effect right away (Bret Victor's instinct, and cards-3d-movie.md's)</span
              >
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="i3">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#i3">I3</a> <span class="plan-title">Explorers as a way to learn</span>
              <span class="goals-note">the Thing Explorer shows the program's world while it runs</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="i4">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#i4">I4</a> <span class="plan-title">"How did spell read this?"</span>
              <span class="goals-note">click a line to see how it was understood, in plain words</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="i5">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#i5">I5</a> <span class="plan-title">Text stays the truth</span>
              <span class="goals-note"
                >dragging a button writes readable spell; the talk: the saved format must be readable</span
              >
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="questions"><ui-icon name="circle question"></ui-icon> 5. Questions</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="question">
            <li data-status="open" id="q1">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#q1">Q1</a> <span class="plan-title">Rebuild the shell on Solid first?</span>
              <span class="goals-note">or add features on React and migrate later</span
              ><ui-accordion class="spell-aside" styled
                ><ui-title>details</ui-title
                ><ui-content
                  ><p>
                    <strong>Suggestion:</strong> build the <em>new</em> shell (project list, file list, modes) on Solid
                    and @spell-app/ui from the start, and move the editor page into it. Adding features to the React
                    shell means building them twice.
                  </p>
                </ui-content></ui-accordion
              >
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="q2">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#q2">Q2</a> <span class="plan-title">What's on the first screen?</span>
              <span class="goals-note">a gallery of examples? a blank card? a guide?</span
              ><ui-accordion class="spell-aside" styled
                ><ui-title>details</ui-title
                ><ui-content
                  ><p>
                    <strong>Suggestion:</strong> a gallery of runnable examples with "Try it" and "See how it works",
                    plus "New project". Matches "read first" (<a target="_self" href="../audience/audience.html#q2"
                      >audience/Q2</a
                    >).
                  </p>
                </ui-content></ui-accordion
              >
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="q3">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#q3">Q3</a> <span class="plan-title">How does dragging map to text?</span>
              <span class="goals-note">does dropping a button write spell, JSX, or a layout file?</span
              ><ui-accordion class="spell-aside" styled
                ><ui-title>details</ui-title
                ><ui-content
                  ><p>See <a target="_self" href="../syntax/syntax.html#q4">syntax/Q4</a>.</p>
                </ui-content></ui-accordion
              >
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="q4">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#q4">Q4</a> <span class="plan-title">Web app, desktop app, or both?</span>
              <span class="goals-note">and a hosted playground?</span
              ><ui-accordion class="spell-aside" styled
                ><ui-title>details</ui-title
                ><ui-content
                  ><p>
                    See <a target="_self" href="../native/native.html">native</a>. Suggestion: one codebase, three
                    homes.
                  </p>
                </ui-content></ui-accordion
              >
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="q5">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#q5">Q5</a> <span class="plan-title">Monaco or CodeMirror?</span>
              <span class="goals-note"
                >Monaco is heavy and desktop-only; CodeMirror 6 is lighter and works on phones</span
              ><ui-accordion class="spell-aside" styled
                ><ui-title>details</ui-title
                ><ui-content
                  ><p>
                    <strong>Context:</strong> the app moved from CodeMirror to Monaco on 2026-09-27. Monaco brings the
                    VS Code feel; CodeMirror 6 would suit embeds and tablets.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    <strong>Suggestion:</strong> keep Monaco for the app; revisit for
                    <a target="_self" href="../web-components/web-components.html">web-components</a>.
                  </p>
                </ui-content></ui-accordion
              >
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="q6">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#q6">Q6</a> <span class="plan-title">How visible is the parser?</span>
              <span class="goals-note">AST and match panes: a developer mode only?</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="risks"><ui-icon name="triangle exclamation"></ui-icon> 6. Risks</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="risk">
            <li data-status="open" id="r1">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#r1">R1</a> <span class="plan-title">The rewrite trap</span>
              <span class="goals-note">migrating and adding features at once</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="r2">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#r2">R2</a> <span class="plan-title">A server that trusts its browser</span>
              <span class="goals-note">fine locally; a hosted app needs real safety</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="r3">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#r3">R3</a> <span class="plan-title">Monaco's weight</span>
              <span class="goals-note">slow first load; no phones or tablets</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="decisions"><ui-icon name="gavel"></ui-icon> 7. Decisions</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="decision"></ol>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="work"><ui-icon name="list check"></ui-icon> 8. Work</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ol class="plan-items" data-kind="work">
            <li data-status="open" id="w1">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#w1">W1</a> <span class="plan-title">Projects in a user folder</span>
              <span class="goals-note">make the projects root configurable; "duplicate this example"</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="w2">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#w2">W2</a> <span class="plan-title">Hide the developer panes</span>
              <span class="goals-note">AST and match viewers behind a setting</span>
            </li>
            <li data-status="open" id="w3">
              <a class="plan-id" href="#w3">W3</a> <span class="plan-title">Fix the server's suspected bugs</span>
              <span class="goals-note">locking, error responses: agents/SUSPECTED-BUGS.md, spell §2</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="s2">
          <ui-sticky class="spell-h2"
            ><h2 id="history"><ui-icon name="clock rotate left"></ui-icon> 9. History</h2></ui-sticky
          >
          <ui-feed class="spell-history goals-history" size="small"
            ><ui-event icon="pen to square"
              ><ui-content
                ><ui-summary
                  >Page made: a first pass from the code, the 2017 talk and old notes
                  <ui-date>2026-10-01</ui-date></ui-summary
                ></ui-content
              ></ui-event
            ></ui-feed
          >
        </section>

        <footer class="spell-doc-footer">
          <ui-divider></ui-divider>
          <p class="meta">
            Part of the <a href="../index.html" target="_self">spell</a> goal set. Notes for agents:
            <a href="app.md" target="src-goals-app-app-md">app.md</a>.
          </p>
        </footer>
      </main>
    </div>
